# {{.project_name}}

Native local-first Rust desktop app generated by smokeforge.

## Stack

- egui / eframe 0.37, egui_tiles, egui_extras, egui_plot, egui_notify
- Rust 1.96, Tokio 1.54, reqwest 0.13 with rustls
- rusqlite 0.40, r2d2_sqlite, refinery migrations
- keyring 4.2, tracing, directories, rust-i18n
- cargo-packager 0.11

## Commands

```bash
make dev-tools     # once: install the pinned cargo-watch
make dev           # run and rebuild + restart on every save
make watch-check   # cargo check on every save
make watch-test    # tests on every save
make run           # run once
make check
make test
make lint
make package
```

See [docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) for what triggers a rebuild,
what survives a restart, and watch-mode troubleshooting.

`make run` and `make dev` install a local desktop entry on Linux so the Smoke icon appears in the desktop shell. Packaged builds use the bundled icon.

Read `CONTEXT.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `docs/LIBRARIES.md`, and `docs/DOCKER.md` before changing code.

## Component work

Read `.agents/skills/egui-component-engineering/SKILL.md` before adding or changing UI. It defines the reusable component contract, stable-ID rules, keyboard/accessibility bar, theme-token policy, and verification gate. The template also vendors `rust-async-patterns`, `rust-patterns`, `rust-testing`, and the two Rust best-practice skills from the API template.

